From: Robert Vokac <robertvokac@robertvokac.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] GPU: clamp each Vulkan mip level's blit extent to one texel

VULKAN_GenerateMipmaps sized each level's blit as width >> level and
height >> level, so in a non-square chain the shorter side reached 0
before the last level: generating the mips of an 8x2 texture blitted an
8x0 region into level 2 and a 0x0 one into level 3, which writes nothing
and leaves those levels as they were (zero for a fresh render target).
Levels are at least one texel per side, as D3D12_GenerateMipmaps already
clamps them with SDL_max(..., 1).

Not an upstream commit: SDL main still sizes them unclamped (checked
2026-10-26 at 52289a276). Carried by CNA (2026-10-26 remediation review:
FNA3D's SDL_GPU driver resolves mipmapped render targets with
SDL_GenerateMipmapsForGPUTexture).
---
--- a/src/gpu/vulkan/SDL_gpu_vulkan.c
+++ b/src/gpu/vulkan/SDL_gpu_vulkan.c
@@ -9305,16 +9305,16 @@
             blit.srcOffsets[0].y = 0;
             blit.srcOffsets[0].z = depth;
 
-            blit.srcOffsets[1].x = container->header.info.width >> (level - 1);
-            blit.srcOffsets[1].y = container->header.info.height >> (level - 1);
+            blit.srcOffsets[1].x = SDL_max(container->header.info.width >> (level - 1), 1);
+            blit.srcOffsets[1].y = SDL_max(container->header.info.height >> (level - 1), 1);
             blit.srcOffsets[1].z = depth + 1;
 
             blit.dstOffsets[0].x = 0;
             blit.dstOffsets[0].y = 0;
             blit.dstOffsets[0].z = depth;
 
-            blit.dstOffsets[1].x = container->header.info.width >> level;
-            blit.dstOffsets[1].y = container->header.info.height >> level;
+            blit.dstOffsets[1].x = SDL_max(container->header.info.width >> level, 1);
+            blit.dstOffsets[1].y = SDL_max(container->header.info.height >> level, 1);
             blit.dstOffsets[1].z = depth + 1;
 
             blit.srcSubresource.aspectMask = VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_COLOR_BIT;
